Circle and Sphere Calculator in C
About the Project

This is a simple mathematical calculator developed using the C programming language. 
The program asks the user to enter the radius and calculates the area of a circle, the surface area of a sphere, and the volume of a sphere.

Concepts Learned

Through this project, I practised the following C programming concepts:

Variables: Declaring and initializing variables using double.
Constants: Using const to declare a constant value of PI.
User Input: Using scanf() to get the radius from the user.
Output: Using printf() to display calculated results.
Format Specifiers: Using %lf for reading double values and %.2lf for displaying results up to two decimal places.
Mathematical Operations: Performing multiplication, division, and exponentiation.
Math Library: Using math.h and the pow() function to calculate powers.
Formulas: Applying mathematical formulas in a C program.
Formulas Used
Area of a Circle: Area = π × r²
Surface Area of a Sphere: Surface Area = 4 × π × r²
Volume of a Sphere: Volume = (4/3) × π × r³

Where:
π = 3.14159
r = Radius

How the Program Works
The program asks the user to enter the radius.
It calculates the area of the circle.
It calculates the surface area of the sphere.
It calculates the volume of the sphere.
Finally, it displays all three results with two decimal places.
What I Learned

This project helped me understand how to use mathematical formulas in C, work with double data types, use constants, perform calculations using the math library, and display formatted numerical output.
